title:open_brain
tags:
---
Now that you have all basic knowledge of the brain lobes and its internals, lets understand some less-known funfacts about the brain. #line:05ebfc8 

Look at the open skull below. The brain parts are color coded again to help to know better about the brain fun-facts according to your previous learning. #line:0f19859 

The human body besides the brain model, will help us to understand which part of the brain controls which part of the body. #line:04d55ee 

Keep an eye out and your ears attentive as we explore these fascinating facts together. The human body part will light up as we discuss the corresponding brain part. #line:0084d62 

<<jump FunFacts>>

=== 

title:FunFacts
tags: 
--- 

Let's start with the right brain often referred to as right hemisphere. #line:078a6d3 

<<RightBrainHighlight YarnCommands>>

The right brain is known as the “creative brain”, linked to art, music, and imagination. #line:040178a 
<<deRightBrainHighlight YarnCommands>>
It controls the left side of your body – so if you’re left-handed, your right brain is working extra hard. #line:0da6532 
<<RightSideBodyHighlight YarnCommands>>
The right brain loves patterns and spatial awareness – which is why you can recognize faces so quickly. #line:051026f 
<<deRightSideBodyHighlight YarnCommands>>
It processes things in a holistic, big-picture way – zooming out instead of zooming in. #line:05a94aa 

The right brain is great at picking up emotions and tone in someone’s voice – your built-in “vibe detector". #line:0bf913d 



Now, let's move to the left brain, or left hemisphere. #line:0cc6eb9 

<<LeftBrainHighlight YarnCommands>>

The left brain is often called the “analytical brain”, famous for logic, numbers, and reasoning. #line:0d721a3 
<<deLeftBrainHighlight YarnCommands>>
It controls the right side of your body – so when you write with your right hand, thank your left brain! #line:0e8772f 
<<LeftSideBodyHighlight YarnCommands>>
Language and grammar? That’s the left brain’s specialty – it’s like your inner grammar police. #line:0bba602 
<<deLeftSideBodyHighlight YarnCommands>>
It processes information in a linear, step-by-step way – like following a recipe. #line:0a6f3d5 

